<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC lowers cash bond rates.</title>
<headline>SBC lowers cash bond rates.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp (SBC) said it was lowering the interest rate it pays on some of its cash bonds (kassenobligationen) with effect from Monday, September 30. SBC gave the following details:</p>
<p> Cash bonds	    New Rate	   Previous</p>
<p> Two-year		2.0 pct	    2.5 pct</p>
<p> Three-year	    2.5 pct	    3.0 pct</p>
<p> Four-year	     3.0 pct	    3.25 pct</p>
<p> Five-year	     3.25 pct	   3.50 pct</p>
<p> Six-year		3.50 pct	   3.75 pct</p>
<p> Seven-year	    3.75 pct	   4.0 pct</p>
<p> Eight-year	    4.0 pct	    4.25 pct</p>
<p>Note - Cash bonds, fixed-rate deposits for small investors, are used by banks to help finance their mortgage lending. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
